+
+Reading from a file
+~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
+
+The :func:`~rich.progress.open` function works like the builtin ``open``, but shows a progress bar while the file is read. It returns a context manager that starts the display on entry and stops it on exit. By default the file is opened in text mode, so ``read()`` returns a ``str``. The total is the size of the file in bytes::
+
+    from rich.progress import open
+
+    with open("data.txt") as text_file:
+        contents = text_file.read()
+
+Pass ``"rb"`` as the mode to read bytes instead. The reader returns ``bytes``::
+
+    from rich.progress import open
+
+    with open("data.bin", "rb") as binary_file:
+        data = binary_file.read()
+
+The :meth:`~rich.progress.Progress.open` method does the same work on an existing :class:`~rich.progress.Progress` instance. It attaches a reader to a new task, or to a task you pass in with ``task_id``. It does not start the display, so the enclosing ``with Progress()`` block does that::
+
+    from rich.progress import Progress
+
+    with Progress() as progress:
+        with progress.open("data.txt") as text_file:
+            contents = text_file.read()
+
+
+Reading from a file-like object
+~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
+
+If you already have an open binary file object, use :func:`~rich.progress.wrap_file`. Only binary file objects are supported, and ``total`` (the size in bytes) is required. The reader does not close the file you pass in, so the file stays open after the ``with`` block::
+
+    import os
+    from rich.progress import wrap_file
+
+    path = "data.bin"
+    with open(path, "rb") as source:
+        with wrap_file(source, total=os.path.getsize(path)) as binary_file:
+            data = binary_file.read()
+
+:meth:`~rich.progress.Progress.wrap_file` is the method form. It can also reuse an existing task, in which case ``total`` may be omitted if the task already has one. This applies only to the method, not to :func:`~rich.progress.wrap_file`::
+
+    import os
+    from rich.progress import Progress
+
+    path = "data.bin"
+    with Progress() as progress:
+        task_id = progress.add_task("Parsing", total=os.path.getsize(path))
+        with open(path, "rb") as source:
+            data = progress.wrap_file(source, task_id=task_id).read()
+
